  "answer": "For pricing questions, the best context strategy is to treat the official pricing schedule as the sole source of truth, because NL-003 declares itself the sole source of truth for proposals, renewals, and audits and forbids using historical or informal pricing models [NL-003#NL-003-S01].  \nFor metrics questions, the best strategy is to rely on official business-metrics reports rather than the sales playbook, using NL-012, NL-016, and NL-001 for churn, NPS, revenue, and segment data [NL-012#NL-012-S09], [NL-016#NL-016-S03], [NL-001#NL-001-S04].  \nFor cross-document business recommendations, the best strategy is reconciliation with conflict resolution: when sales-playbook or call-narrative claims conflict with official metrics, defer to the metrics evidence. For example, NL-016 explicitly corrects NL-009’s earlier emphasis on startups, showing SMBs have high churn and weak retention versus regulated mid-market and enterprise segments [NL-016#NL-016-S03], and NL-023’s note flags a seller’s startup-friendly claim against official SMB churn data [NL-023#NL-023-S03]. This prevents recommendations from being based on outdated or non-authoritative narrative content.\n\nANSWER_STATUS: answer  \nUSED_MEMORY_CLAIMS: none",
